# DC-1 amber frontlight node setup.
#
# Gate 3 of 3 for rootless amber control: the kernel node is root:root 0644,
# so even with the TE allow + mlstrustedobject (sepolicy/dc1amber.te) the
# app's write fails EACCES on plain DAC. init opens the mode; SELinux still
# restricts writers to the domains policy allows (hal_light, init,
# platform_app, system_app).
#
# The early write also lights the frontlight out of the box: on a fresh
# /data the AmberControl package can still be in the first-boot "stopped"
# state, which excludes it from BOOT_COMPLETED, so init seeds full amber
# (Daylight UI scale: 255 = max) and the app takes over once launched.

on post-fs-data
    chmod 0666 /sys/class/leds/lcd-backlight-amber/brightness
    write /sys/class/leds/lcd-backlight-amber/brightness 255

on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    chmod 0666 /sys/class/leds/lcd-backlight-amber/brightness
